{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And Israel saw the great hand</b> — the great might that the hand of HaKadosh Baruch Hu performed. Many expressions fall upon the word יד, and all of them are literally the expression 'hand'; the one who corrects should correct the expression according to the context. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 14:31). But Onkelos (Onkelos on Exodus 14:31) did not explain <b>the great hand</b> as 'might,' but rather said 'the might of the great hand.' And Rabbi Abraham Ibn Ezra said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 14:31) 'the great blow,' and so too 'behold, the hand of YHWH will be upon your livestock' (Exodus 9:3), 'the hand of Elohim was very heavy there' (I Samuel 5:11). And by way of truth, one should say that <b>the great hand</b> was revealed to them, and it is the attribute of judgment that YHWH executed in Egypt, for there was a blow against them in Egypt; and this is like 'and on earth He showed you His great fire' (Deuteronomy 4:36), and it is the right hand with which You shatter the enemy, and it is the arm of YHWH of which Scripture says, 'Awake, awake, put on strength, O arm of YHWH' (Isaiah 51:9), 'Was it not You who hewed the sea?' (ibid. v. 10). And it will not be hidden from you what is meant by 'put on strength,' from what we have written on the verse 'from the hand of the Mighty One of Jacob' (Genesis 49:24)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The acronym הקב״ה is resolved as HaKadosh Baruch Hu; 'Rabbi Abraham Ibn Ezra' renders ר״א; the repeated phrase 'and so too' is rendered once for the first citation chain and the second biblical citation follows with 'and so too' implied."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:08:18.492056971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}